      "message": "feat(contour): user-set exit point on closed 2D contours\n\nThe ring nearest links.approach.exit_point is cut all the way round,\nthen on along its own cutter-centre polyline to the pick's projection,\nand the lead-out leaves there. A lead-out that does not fit there, a\nlead-in the longer walk loses, a lead-out crossing the lead-in, tabs,\ncontrol compensation, the keep-down level link, an overlap beside it,\nopen chains, tilted contours and other kinds are refused by name.\nAlso pins the picked start's \"no lead-in fits\" refusal (PR 1478 review).\n\nRefs #1473\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
